{
  "sn12.4:0.1": "Linked Discourses 12.4 ",
  "sn12.4:0.2": "1. The Buddhas ",
  "sn12.4:0.3": "About Vipassī ",
  "sn12.4:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn12.4:1.2": "“Mendicants, Vipassī the Blessed One, the perfected one, the fully awakened Buddha had this thought before his awakening, when he was still unawakened but intent on awakening: ",
  "sn12.4:1.3": "‘Alas, this world has fallen into trouble. It’s born, grows old, dies, passes away, and is reborn, ",
  "sn12.4:1.4": "yet it doesn’t understand how to escape from this suffering, from old age and death. ",
  "sn12.4:1.5": "Oh, when will an escape be found from this suffering, from old age and death?’ ",
  "sn12.4:2.1": "Then Vipassī, the one intent on awakening, thought: ",
  "sn12.4:2.2": "‘When what exists is there old age and death? What is a requirement for old age and death?’ ",
  "sn12.4:2.3": "Then, through rational application of mind, Vipassī penetrated with wisdom: ",
  "sn12.4:2.4": "‘When rebirth exists there’s old age and death. Rebirth is a requirement for old age and death.’ ",
  "sn12.4:3.1": "Then Vipassī thought: ",
  "sn12.4:3.2": "‘When what exists is there rebirth? What is a requirement for rebirth?’ ",
  "sn12.4:3.3": "Then, through rational application of mind, Vipassī penetrated with wisdom: ",
  "sn12.4:3.4": "‘When continued existence exists there’s rebirth. Continued existence is a requirement for rebirth.’ ",
  "sn12.4:4.1": "Then Vipassī thought: ",
